      equipment: 'Usually a 32-card German deck (7 to Ace) or a standard 52-card deck.',
      dealing: 'All cards are dealt out evenly to the players face-down. Players may not look at their cards.',
    },
    turnFlow: "1. Players take turns flipping one card face-up onto a central pile in a rhythmic fashion.\n2. **The Chant**: As each card is played, the current player says a rank in ascending order: 'Seven', 'Eight', 'Nine', 'Ten', 'Jack', 'Queen', 'King', 'Ace', then repeats.\n3. **The Kloepper (Knock)**: If the card revealed matches the rank being spoken, all players must immediately slap their hand onto the central pile.\n4. **Penalty**: The last player to slap takes the entire pile of cards and adds it to their personal stack.\n5. **Fake-Outs**: If a player slaps the pile when no match has occurred, they take the pile as a penalty.",
